The factory stores classes (not instances) in a dict and calls only the one selected, which avoids constructing products that are not used. The shared `set_volume` lives in the abstract parent. One weakness to discuss: an unknown format makes `.get(type_)` return `None`, and calling `None(...)` raises an unhelpful `TypeError`.

**`audio/products.py`**

